      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the breakdown. but it feels like you're kind of balancing them now, whereas your first answer was pretty definitive about restorative justice being \"more morally sound.\" if we're looking at it through the lens of modern social justice, isn't the retributive model basically just an outdated, systemic tool of oppression that doesn't actually achieve justice? shouldn't we see it more as an obstacle to progress rather than a valid alternative?",
